d implementation of modern and progressive work practices to facilitate improved employee performance and efficiency; and\n\nWHEREAS the well-being of employees and efficient administration of the Govern","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-opus_zip-11491-2509b59a45.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"7d9eacc34924b4c100afc56f9c97fa485fd5d18f5da32a0c7a9929c8f111c9b1","source":{"line":6909,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"dd83dcb1ff6f83382ca85ae227d3cfbab26f4f434b2c0deb2c9e1e7fe4348698"}},{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"t","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"db3e7966c86bf015e11638031156112944d0b0fb96a2d7dd0e00324b4eada8a2"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:11491\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-10-31/pdf/FR-1969-10-31.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: c6ecd90564b8b1d8d14a17d5fa63f91ec41b5b15046a86464a278d30c88592e8\nLocation: 34 FR 17605, PDF pages 5-15 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on ","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_11491.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"634e87e268066dc5e7c57185fd37d84c035c7a56e14c954f995f4a8ea1a0caed","source":{"line":1302,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"ef8362e836480d98d956b93cd0d93f0d16a4e94eb95eef6ab5a6d3b1ff7f15b4"}},{"first_1500_characters":"PART 5b—PRIVACY ACT REGULATIONS\nAuthority:5 U.S.C. 301, 5 U.S.C. 552a. \nSource:45 FR 30808, May 9, 1980, unless otherwise noted. \n§ 5b.1 Definitions.\nAs used in this part: \n(a) Access means availability of a record to a subject individual. \n(b) Agency means the Department of Education. \n(c) Department means the Department of Education. \n(d) Disclosure means the availability or release of a record ","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t34-part5b.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"ca8d4d0b75ad7193c1446e41791b991d42cce88d09d80d596634e5df8a233f33","source":{"line":354,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"a7af96be5e6c1a4ad591be101be54f03a9d1f7d73f368744c1f01d0a306ffdbe"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 251.101 Introduction.\n(a) The regulations in this part apply to all Federal executive branch departments and agencies and their officers and employees.\n(b) This part provides a framework for consulting and communicating with non-labor organizations representing Federal employees and with other organizations on matters related to agency operations and personnel management.\n(c) The purposes of con","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t5-251.101.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"a4e311bfee24de92cc6e6f14e8dee9208bd57da6919f9b07d31cd2434bf1ed59","source":{"line":473,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"7afc5b82a36e950f18265947f123bb1c29067fe34e3a6c69fcd398ebdae0de62"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 550.322 Saving provision.\nAn agency shall permit a supervisor who so desires, to continue an allotment of dues to a labor organization as defined by section 2(e) of Executive Order 11491, as amended, which was permissible when the supervisor was excluded from a formal or exclusive unit by reason of the requirements of former section 24(d) of this Order.\n","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t5-550.322.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"8f13a34faaaf103565d0aeb582f6d0b2cf4d0d4dca1942eec63c0479df9c76c0","source":{"line":491,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"214b1c95007c759b65701cbd4f87a207dffc94ac58a92be30bd7f67334d509ad"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 831.1511 Authorized allottees.\n(a) An annuitant may make an allotment to the national office or headquarters of any of the following organizations: \n(1) A labor organization recognized under Executive Order 11491, as amended; \n(2) An employee organization recognized under 5 U.S.C. 8901(8); \n(3) Other lawful organizations which: \n(i) Are national in scope, \n(ii) Are nonprofit and noncommercial, e","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t5-831.1511.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"20e76e418891e69ef7d0e26e11bbdc8d25616e20dddfef98c262b91c63e2fa04","source":{"line":500,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"ccf445b6886b8d8e4de4afe1bca2dcaf68f60de1113a022c1ff99d25a2f75415"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 9701.526 Continuation of existing laws, recognitions, agreements, and procedures.\n(a) Except as otherwise provided by § 9701.506, nothing contained in this subpart precludes the renewal or continuation of an exclusive recognition, certification of an exclusive representative, or an agreement that is otherwise consistent with law and the regulations in this part between the Department or a compon","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t5-9701.526.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"d2abcd40e1cea2c4a7ae5568e58ef93b5ae994e862e0d201663887e36abb8be2","source":{"line":504,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"65c0c91ec29a814d2300e5b64904f4340c2274b02e77913fee4d95b7b448cd89"}},{"first_1500_characters":"PART 251—AGENCY RELATIONSHIPS WITH ORGANIZATIONS REPRESENTING FEDERAL EMPLOYEES AND OTHER ORGANIZATIONS\nAuthority:5 U.S.C. 1104; 5 U.S.C. Chap 7; 5 U.S.C. 7135; 5 U.S.C. 7301; and E.O. 11491.\nSource:61 FR 32915, June 26, 1996, unless otherwise noted.\nSubpart A—General Provisions\n§ 251.101 Introduction.\n(a) The regulations in this part apply to all Federal executive branch departments and agencies ","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t5-part251.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"94f6f62421474fa0d8fed83a2cab9f27df5bf20f5eace861045fa6d3ab58de7a","source":{"line":514,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"77b288bb7b842739d15e0d29e3bd32b3f4d5e922606a4ba1a1ca56ec5050e878"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 7101.\n Findings and purpose\n(a)\n The Congress finds that—\n(1)\n experience in both private and public employment indicates that the statutory protection of the right of employees to organize, bargain collectively, and participate through labor organizations of their own choosing in decisions which affect them—\n(A)\n safeguards the public interest,\n(B)\n contributes to the effective conduct of publi","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/usc-t5-s7101.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"6fb75062fd1988dc4c78619a9bb58fa264d505ee6d864cdf73b5c608f5ba450d","source":{"line":1440,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"50bb702177bce4344c399977a83cb5329c17b2299802ca84a8cb5b639ea65e37"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 7135.\n Continuation of existing laws, recognitions, agreements, and procedures\n(a)\n Nothing contained in this chapter shall preclude—\n(1)\n the renewal or continuation of an exclusive recognition, certification of an exclusive representative, or a lawful agreement between an agency and an exclusive representative of its employees, which is entered into before the effective date of this chapter; o","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/usc-t5-s7135.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"1f0cb3cc9026e0ccac6e6a3ff86e64161bc29d35eadc9c1c51b2824ddbc1c910","source":{"line":1442,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"bd1b4a4a97182dc468693b4a97480295c949ba1d1a128e7c699b57fdc3aa81aa"}}]}
